      "stem": "$9^x + 4(3^x) - 12$",
      "final_answer": "$(3^x + 6)(3^x - 2)$",
      "mark_breakdown": [
        {
          "code": "M1",
          "desc": "Treating as a quadratic in $3^x$"
        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "desc": "Correct factorization"
        }
      ],
      "solution": "9^x + 4(3^x) - 12 = (3^x)^2 + 4(3^x) - 12 = (3^x + 6)(3^x - 2)",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "Quadratic substitution: Let $u = 3^x$, then $9^x = u^2$.",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Express as $u^2 + 4u - 12$.",
          "Find two numbers that multiply to $-12$ and add to $4$: $+6$ and $-2$.",
          "Factorize: $(u + 6)(u - 2) = (3^x + 6)(3^x - 2)$."
        ],
        "common_pitfalls": "Forgetting to substitute $3^x$ back in place of $u$."
      }
    },
